    "q-268174": {
      "dom_id": "step-q268174",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the function $f,$ defined as \n\n$$\nf({x}_{1},{x}_{2})={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the shape of the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "The total derivative of a scalar-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the row vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ and\n\n- outputs a scalar $f({x}_{1},{x}_{2})\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the total derivative will be a row vector of shape $1\\times 2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-268174-a",
