    "q-269269": {
      "dom_id": "step-q269269",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the function $f,$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the shape of the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$",
      "worked_solution": "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:R\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a scalar $x$ is the column vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times 1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a scalar $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- outputs a vector $f(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the total derivative will be a column vector of shape $2\\times 1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
