    "q-269512": {
      "dom_id": "step-q269512",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Consider the function $f:R\\to {R}^{3},$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ {x}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$",
      "worked_solution": "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:R\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a scalar $x$ is the column vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times 1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a scalar $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- outputs a vector $f(x)\\in {R}^{3}$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ {x}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2x \\\\ 3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{3\\times 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
