    "q-269508": {
      "dom_id": "step-q269508",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Consider the function $f:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.$ What is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "The total derivative of a scalar-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the row vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3},$ and\n\n- outputs a scalar $f(x)\\in R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)={x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{3} & 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times 3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the total derivative at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}({x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}0+3(2) & 1+2 & 3(1)+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
