    "q-269665": {
      "dom_id": "step-q269665",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to {R}^{2}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]A.\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{a}_{22}}=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{11}-2{a}_{21}+3{a}_{31} & 2{a}_{12}-2{a}_{22}+3{a}_{32}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{a}_{22}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{22}}(2{a}_{12}-2{a}_{22}+3{a}_{32})=-2.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
