    "q-269667": {
      "dom_id": "step-q269667",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to {R}^{2}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]A.\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{a}_{32}}=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{11}+{a}_{21}-2{a}_{31} & 5{a}_{12}+{a}_{22}-2{a}_{32}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{a}_{32}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{32}}(5{a}_{11}+{a}_{21}-2{a}_{31})=0.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
