    "q-269655": {
      "dom_id": "step-q269655",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 3}\\to {R}^{3}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=A[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{31}}=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{11}+{a}_{12}+4{a}_{13} \\\\ 5{a}_{21}+{a}_{22}+4{a}_{23} \\\\ 5{a}_{31}+{a}_{32}+4{a}_{33}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{31}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{31}}(5{a}_{31}+{a}_{32}+4{a}_{33})=5.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
