    "q-269669": {
      "dom_id": "step-q269669",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 3}\\to {R}^{3}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 & -5\\end{aligned}]A.\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{33}}=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10{a}_{11}-6{a}_{21}-5{a}_{31}\\, & 10{a}_{12}-6{a}_{22}-5{a}_{32}\\, & 10{a}_{13}-6{a}_{23}-5{a}_{33}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{33}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{33}}(10{a}_{13}-6{a}_{23}-5{a}_{33})=-5.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
